      "writtenOn": "2023-11-03T03:05:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`TurningOff` means \"waiting for pid file to be deleted\". But in this state we can\u0027t be sure whether the pid file is created or not, so we shouldn\u0027t set `TurningOff`.\n\nThis reminds me that per the current design, `stop` a `TurningOn` adapter should be no-op: `TurningOn` belongs to a disabled state, while the client shouldn\u0027t disable a disabled adapter.\n\nI\u0027m fixing this in this patch as well. (This should be something in https://r.android.com/c/2808093, but it\u0027s already merged)",
      "parentUuid": "fff5e916_4a7f9960",
